Bootstrap: docker
From: ubuntu:16.04

%labels
  MAINTAINER Daniel Dopp <danieldopp@uky.edu>
  VERSION 0.9
  OS Ubuntu 16.04

%post
  # Basic installs
  apt update
  apt install -y git

  # Store git credentials for up to an hour (in overlay, not container) for convenience
  git config --global credential.helper cache
  git config --global credential.helper 'cache --timeout=3600'

  # Required to make python3.7 available
  apt install -y software-properties-common
  add-apt-repository -y ppa:deadsnakes/ppa
  apt update

  # Python installs
  apt install -y python3.7-dev python3-pip
  pip3 install --upgrade pip
  pip install pipenv

  # Set the system to properly read UTF-8 encoded files
  export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
  export LANG=C.UTF-8

  git clone https://code.cs.uky.edu/seales-research/spectral-analysis.git

  # Give read/write access in spectral-analysis (so it can later be edited using a persistent overlay)
  chmod --recursive a+rw /spectral-analysis

  # Create a pipenv for this project with up to data development code
  cd /spectral-analysis

  git checkout development
  git pull origin
  pipenv install

  # Now install spectral-analysis
  pipenv install -e .

%runscript
  # TODO, figure out how to set these permanently in the post section
  export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
  export LANG=C.UTF-8

  if [ $# -lt 1 ]; then
      echo "Usage: ./container <command>"
      exit 1
  fi

  cd /spectral-analysis
  git pull origin

  exec "$@"

%help
  This container provides an environment for running spectral-analysis.

  Building the container:
    - Prerequisite: the spectral-analysis git repository must exist at /spectral-analysis on the host machine before building the container. Https is recommended so that it can be manipulated after container creation using your username and password instead of needing ssh key
    - You may check out a different branch or make changes if desired, but this can all be done after the container is created.
    - Build as usual, for example: sudo singularity build spectral-analysis spectral-analysis.def

  Usage:
    - It is possible to use an overlay to allow one to check out another branch, pull recent changes, or make local edits to spectral-analysis code: `dd if=/dev/zero of=spectral-analysis.overlay bs=1M count=500 && mkfs.ext3 spectral-analysis.overlay; singularity shell --overlay spectral_analysis.overlay

  This container is intended to be built once, and used with many checkouts of spectral-analysis code. Only when the dependencies change does the container need rebuilding.
